phoenix: fix qup_uart3 sleep CTS bias + add WCN3998 SNOC 8-bit cap quirk

Two residual fixes against sm7150-mainline v7.1_rc3 that are not yet
upstream:

1. qup_uart3_sleep cts-pins uses bias-bus-hold, which is invalid on the
   main SM7150 TLMM (only the lpass_tlmm pinctrl supports it).
   bias-bus-hold is silently ignored at runtime, leaving the CTS pin
   floating during sleep and producing intermittent Bluetooth UART
   flow-control glitches. Replace with bias-pull-up to match the
   pin's wakeup/idle direction.

2. WCN3998 on phoenix needs qcom,snoc-host-cap-8bit-quirk; — the
   identification firmware reports a malformed host-cap response that
   ath10k's 16-bit decoder cannot parse, and the 8-bit quirk path is
   required for QMI bring-up.

Signed-off-by: phoenix port <fix@me>

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -802,7 +802,7 @@ &tlmm {
 			pins = "gpio38";
 			function = "gpio";
 			drive-strength = <2>;
-			bias-bus-hold;
+			bias-pull-up;
 		};

 		rts-pins {
@@ -971,5 +971,6 @@ &venus {
 	vdd-3.3-ch0-supply = <&vreg_pmu_ch0>;
 	vdd-3.3-ch1-supply = <&vreg_pmu_ch1>;

+	qcom,snoc-host-cap-8bit-quirk;
 	status = "okay";
 };
